From 5d9a9ea1f04ea5cbae26b771f24c662b9f73ad93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Zero the SAX handler before libxml2 is asked to initialise it

-[GSSAXHandler _initLibXML] allocates its xmlSAXHandler with malloc and
hands it straight to xmlSAX2InitDefaultSAXHandler(), whose first act is

    if ((hdlr == NULL) || (hdlr->initialized != 0)) return;

so whenever the uninitialised `initialized' field happens to be
non-zero the call does nothing at all, and the handler keeps whatever
the heap had in it.

This is not usually visible as a parse failure: _initLibXML goes on to
call xmlSAXVersion(), which re-establishes the standard callbacks. What
it does cost is a read of uninitialised memory on every parse, an
initialisation that silently does nothing, and the remaining fields of
the handler being whatever was in that memory before.

Valgrind names it on any parse that goes through NSXMLParser, since
that builds one of these handlers:

    Conditional jump or move depends on uninitialised value(s)
       at xmlSAX2InitDefaultSAXHandler (libxml2)
       by -[GSSAXHandler _initLibXML]  (GSXML.m:3808)
     Uninitialised value was created by a heap allocation
       at malloc
       by -[GSSAXHandler _initLibXML]  (GSXML.m:3801)

Allocate the handler with calloc instead. It costs nothing here -- one
structure per parser -- and makes the initialisation deterministic.

A reproduction program accompanies this patch rather than a test in
Tests/base: an uninitialised handler struct has no observable effect on
a parse, so there is nothing for a test to assert. Run the program under
valgrind and it reports the uninitialised read on an unpatched library
and is silent with the change.
---
 Source/Additions/GSXML.m | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Additions/GSXML.m b/Source/Additions/GSXML.m
index 00832d5c4..5c7f9728f 100644
--- a/Source/Additions/GSXML.m
+++ b/Source/Additions/GSXML.m
@@ -3798,7 +3798,7 @@ fatalErrorFunction(void *ctx, const unsigned char *msg, ...)
  */
 - (BOOL) _initLibXML
 {
-  lib = (xmlSAXHandler*)malloc(sizeof(xmlSAXHandler));
+  lib = (xmlSAXHandler*)calloc(1, sizeof(xmlSAXHandler));
   if (lib == NULL)
     {
       return NO;
-- 
